  <prompt>
    Execute Track-B batch 4 of FR-TB-01: delete the stale/actively-misleading catalog, seed, doc, and script surface from inventory §5.4/§9 plus the remainder of the migration map's dependency-free delete list. The 2026-02 ERD docs still show `sprk_actiontypeid` which R7 dropped (misleading); the `docs/ai-knowledge/catalogs/` twin diverges from the `.claude/catalogs/` copy; the R4-taxonomy seed JSONs and `Seed-JpsActions.ps1` are superseded/broken. Two §9 items flagged "(verify)" close here with a verify-first ruling. This batch rides alongside wave W-P1-A. Per NFR-08, every deletion is grep/glob-verified with SHOWN output; evidence lands in `notes/track-b/batch-4-evidence.md`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Developer comfortable across docs, PowerShell scripts, seed data, and BFF services — rigorous about verifying a "probably dead" item's liveness before deleting and documenting keep-with-reason rulings.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Every batch-4 item below is deleted (or recorded keep-with-reason), grep/glob-zero shown per deleted item, builds green for any touched code surface, TASK-INDEX updated, and `notes/track-b/batch-4-evidence.md` written.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="design-spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-context">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    <file purpose="task-index">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md</file>
    <file purpose="deadwood-register">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-CODE-INVENTORY.md</file>
    <file purpose="delete-list">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-MIGRATION-MAP.md</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Do not modify files outside the batch list; deadwood only — if a batch item turns out to be live, STOP and record keep-with-reason instead of deleting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">Every retirement verified grep/glob-zero with SHOWN output; no compat shims retained.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">The KEPT catalog copy is `.claude/catalogs/scope-model-index.json` — do NOT delete or modify it here (task 051 refreshes it in the MAIN session). This batch deletes only the `docs/ai-knowledge/catalogs/` twin. If any `.claude/catalogs/` deletion emerges as necessary, it MUST run in the main session — a sub-agent Edit denial on that path is the boundary working, not a bug.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The 2026-02 ERD docs delete NOW (actively misleading); their replacements are authored at P4 by task 052 (FR-P4-03). The gap in between is accepted per the migration map ("replacements authored in P4").</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Verify-first items: `FallbackScopeCatalog`/`FallbackPrompts` and `LoadKnowledgeNodeExecutor` are §9-flagged "(verify)"/placeholder — grep for consumers first; if wired (e.g., to the frozen engine), record keep-with-reason and leave for the task-050 audit.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>catalogs, seed-data, docs-hygiene, track-b</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-MIGRATION-MAP.md</file>
